{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1950418","formula":"C₂H₃ClO","hill":"C2H3ClO","elements":["H","C","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":3.0,"O":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Chloroacetaldehyde","ru":"Хлорацетальдегид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chloroacetaldehyde is an organic compound with the formula ClCH2CHO. Like some related compounds, it is highly electrophilic reagent and a potentially dangerous alkylating agent. The compound is not normally encountered in the anhydrous form, but rather as the hemiacetal (ClCH2CH(OH))2. Chloroacetaldehyde is a metabolite of the antineoplastic ifosfamide and believed to be responsible for some of the toxicity observed with ifosfamide.","ru":"Хлорацетальдегид (монохлорацетальдегид, хлорэтаналь, хлоруксусный альдегид) — хлорорганическое соединение класса альдегидов с одной карбонильной группой с формулой ClCH2CHO. Обычно встречается не в безводной форме, а в виде полуацеталя."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":33,"mass":78.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(C=O)Cl","inchikey":"QSKPIOLLBIHNAC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-chloroacetaldehyde","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"33","atoms":7,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.601,"y":0.613,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.316,"y":0.681,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.586,"y":-0.832,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.871,"y":-0.462,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.806,"y":-1.421,"z":-0.894,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.806,"y":-1.42,"z":0.894,"el":"H"},{"x":1.563,"y":-1.321,"z":-0.001,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,2,1],[1,3,2],[2,3,1],[2,4,1],[2,5,1],[3,6,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1950418","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chloroacetaldehyde","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","ur